        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs(multi-agent): replace legacy allow:true with enabled:true for Discord channel config examples",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSame pattern as #103491 (slack) and #106188 (config-channels). Two Discord channel config examples in docs/concepts/multi-agent.md use `allow: true`, but the strict Zod schemas only accept `enabled: true`.\n\n## Changes\n\n2 replacements in docs/concepts/multi-agent.md:\n\n```diff\n-                    \"222222222222222222\": { allow: true, requireMention: false },\n+                    \"222222222222222222\": { enabled: true, requireMention: false },\n-                    \"333333333333333333\": { allow: true, requireMention: false },\n+                    \"333333333333333333\": { enabled: true, requireMention: false },\n```\n\n## Evidence\n\n`grep -c 'allow: true' docs/concepts/multi-agent.md` returns 0 after fix. All legitimate `allowFrom` fields are preserved unchanged.\n\n## Review\n\n- Manually reviewed and verified\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
